# tools/cp/bench/bench720.p9 -- Cyberpunk 2077's OWN built-in benchmark on
# HobbyOS, 1280x720, on the settings the seeded prefix already carries
# (Custom = the Low row set, Resolution Scaling Off, 1280x720 borderless,
# VSync Off, no cap, RT off).  Run it with
#   P9_SCRIPT=tools/cp/bench/bench720.p9 bash tools/cp/p9/run-p9.sh
# and extract the game's own files from the run's cpdata.img afterwards with
# tools/cp/bench/extract-bench.sh.  docs/cp-bench.md is the report.
#
# The sequence is tools/cp/p0host/nav.py's, measured on the host-native column
# (game 2.5, 2026-11-14): main menu -> SETTINGS -> '3' (GRAPHICS tab) -> 'b'
# (RUN BENCHMARK) -> Return on "Are you sure you would like to run a
# benchmark?" -> the game's own results page.  On HobbyOS the settings page
# opens on its last-used tab (SOUND CONTROLS on the user's prefix) and the
# OCR header lists every tab, so judge the tab by its page rows; '3' did reach
# GRAPHICS and 'b' triggers RUN BENCHMARK from any tab either way
# (docs/cp-bench.md §5.3).
#
# Nothing here changes a setting: the run measures what the user's profile
# already has, and the screens are captured as the record of it.
#
# v2 (what this file is): the results wait matches "Average FPS" only.
# The 2026-11-24 run used v1, whose pattern also matched the bare word
# "Results"; it fired a frame early, the script went on to quit while the
# benchmark was still flying, the game ignored the input anyway, and the run
# ended with verdict `seek-failed:menu-quit` with the results screen and
# summary.json captured (docs/cp-bench.md §5.2).  The live HUD says "FPS: nn",
# never "Average FPS", so this pattern cannot fire during the flight.

phase menu
shot menu
# ---- main menu -> SETTINGS (main menu rows: CONTINUE .. SETTINGS at y=581) ---
seek menu-settings main down 6 SETTINGS
key ret
wait 4
shot settings-open
# ---- the settings page: 'b' is RUN BENCHMARK from any tab ------------------
key 3
key 3
key 3
wait 3
shot settings-graphics
expect graphics-tab 20 GRAPHICS|Quick\s*Preset|Ray\s*Tracing|BENCHMARK
# ---- run the game's own benchmark ------------------------------------------
phase bench
mark benchmark requested (b on the settings page)
key b
expect bench-confirm 25 LIKE\s*TO\s*RUN|RUN\s*A\s*BENCHMARK|Are\s*you\s*sure
shot bench-confirm
key ret
wait 5
shot bench-running
expect bench-results 900 Average\s*FPS
shot bench-results
wait 10
shot bench-results2
mark BENCHMARK RESULTS ON SCREEN
# ---- back out and quit (the result files are already on the ext2 prefix) ----
# the results page's own EXIT BENCHMARK dialog asks "Do you want to go back to
# the Main Menu?"; Esc opens it, Return answers it.
phase quit
key esc
wait 4
shot after-results
seek menu-quit main down 8 QUIT GAME
exit_ok
phase quit
key ret
wait 3
shot quit-confirm
expect quit-confirm 10 sure.{0,20}quit
key ret
wait_exit 180
